  "content": {
    "id": "p7-p2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Suppose $a^2+b^2=7ab$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-p2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Simplify $\\left(\\dfrac{a+b}{3}\\right)^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$ab$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{a+b}{3}\\right)^2&=\\frac{a^2+2ab+b^2}{9}\\\\\\left(\\frac{a+b}{3}\\right)^2&=\\frac{7ab+2ab}{9}\\\\\\left(\\frac{a+b}{3}\\right)^2&=\\frac{9ab}{9}\\\\\\left(\\frac{a+b}{3}\\right)^2&=ab.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-p2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Assume $a>0$ and $b>0$. Hence, show that\n$$\\log\\left(\\frac{a+b}{3}\\right)=\\frac12\\bigl(\\log(a)+\\log(b)\\bigr).$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\log\\left(\\dfrac{a+b}{3}\\right)=\\dfrac12\\bigl(\\log(a)+\\log(b)\\bigr)$\n\nUse the power law with part (a), then expand $\\log(ab)$ using the product law.",
          "worked": "Since $a$ and $b$ are positive, $\\dfrac{a+b}{3}>0$. Use the result from part (a).\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log\\left(\\frac{a+b}{3}\\right)&=\\frac12\\log\\left[\\left(\\frac{a+b}{3}\\right)^2\\right]\\\\\\log\\left(\\frac{a+b}{3}\\right)&=\\frac12\\log(ab)\\\\\\log\\left(\\frac{a+b}{3}\\right)&=\\frac12\\bigl(\\log(a)+\\log(b)\\bigr).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
